  "worked_solution": "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n6+x-{x}^{2}>0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*greater than*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola  \n\n$$\ny=6+x-{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nis *above* the $x$-axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/40fea084b16f1bf9b1274351377d7608e5f2b505eecc81c5dc23a6fc30edb77b.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $-2<x<3.$",
